####################################################################
# cat3a_cardiorespiratory_arrest.rq — CAT3a, clinical event
# CardioRespiratoryArrest. HAND-AUTHORED.
#
# Criterion (FRAMEWORK/KNOWLEDGE_BASE/clinicalEvents.ttl):
#   evidencedBy some CardiacArrest, and evidencedBy some RespiratoryArrest
# — both events of this patient, both current (hence overlapping). The
# combined event runs from the later constituent start to the earlier
# constituent end. Requires the rules cardiac_arrest and respiratory_arrest.
#
# A DELIBERATE DEPARTURE from the NL rule table (decided 2026-09-21). The
# table reads: "If alarms conveying [reduced heart rate, reduced respiratory
# rate] occur within a 60s timeframe, they collectively convey a respiratory
# arrest." Implemented instead, and the wording the table should carry: "If
# a cardiac arrest (asystole) and a respiratory arrest (apnoea) are present
# at the same time, they collectively convey a cardiorespiratory arrest."
# Clause by clause:
#   "reduced heart rate"       -> a CardiacArrest condition: a heart-rate
#                                 metric with an ABSENT rhythm (asystole).
#                                 Strict on purpose: faithful to clinical
#                                 practice rather than to the table.
#   "reduced respiratory rate" -> a RespiratoryArrest condition: a
#                                 respiration-rate metric with an ABSENT
#                                 rhythm (apnoea).
#   "within a 60s timeframe"   -> both conditions active at the same moment;
#                                 no tolerance window. Sub-analysis on
#                                 DATA_LOCKED: overlap alone gives 929
#                                 episodes in 199 patients; a 60 s window
#                                 would add 44 patients — not needed to
#                                 show the rule triggers.
#   "respiratory arrest"       -> CardioRespiratoryArrest. RespiratoryArrest
#                                 is a condition in its own right, and a
#                                 constituent here.
# Conditions are uniform labels: evidence from any source that meets the
# criterion creates the same condition, so CAT3a combines conditions,
# never specific alarms.
#
# CONTRACT. Bound on entry: ?patient, ?now. Binds: ?evidence and ?support
# (one row per constituent event; the log resolves a constituent event to
# its alarms). Used by the episode actions.
#
# VALIDATION — engine/regression.py: cat3a_pos, cat3c (arrival order
# swapped) and cat3a_withdraw (from the CAT1b withdrawal on) fire;
# cat3a_neg (20 s gap) and cat3a_flagged (CAT1a-flagged asystole) do not.
####################################################################

PREFIX mda:           <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX rdf:           <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX clinicalEvent: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/clinical-event/>

# a current cardiac arrest of this patient
GRAPH ?gCa { ?ca rdf:type clinicalEvent:CardiacArrest . ?ca mda:concernsPatient ?patient .
             FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ca mda:hasEnd ?ca_end } }
# a current respiratory arrest of this patient
GRAPH ?gRa { ?ra rdf:type clinicalEvent:RespiratoryArrest . ?ra mda:concernsPatient ?patient .
             FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ra mda:hasEnd ?ra_end } }
VALUES ?which { 1 2 }
BIND(IF(?which = 1, ?ca, ?ra) AS ?evidence)
BIND(?evidence AS ?support)
